WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:08.367
-I gained 70 pounds
for this film.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.634
-Did you really?
-I mean, I gained it

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:13.334
like 20 years ago, but...

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.601
-You're lactose intolerant!
We can't!

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.167
-[ Sings operatic note ]

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.033
[ Rasping ] I can't breathe.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.067
-Okay, I trust all of you,
especially you, Gloria Steinem.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.834
You're like, "Heeey, hey."

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.567
We have taken on some sponsors,
but some of them are...

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.033
pretty terrible sponsors.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:31.100
Wet Confetti.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.534
No more waiting 'til the end
of the party

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:33.968
to scrape wet confetti
off the floor

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.868
because Wet Confetti is wet
from the very beginning.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.000
The party might be over,
but you still got clean up

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.534
that Wet Confetti.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.734
I've heard one of the keys to
the success in the longevity

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.100
of the Roots over 30 years
is two tour busses.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.267
-Yeah, at least.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.501
-And how does it split up?
Who goes where?

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.501
-Cool people go where I go.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.634
My bus is the --

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.100
We're the dweeb bus.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.901
-Whack!
And look at this.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:02.133
I put a frying pan on his chest.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.434
So, I hit him and he goes,
"Nooooo!"

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:08.567
-Don't forget about
Noice Cancelling Headphones.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.334
If there's one thing
we all can't stand

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.834
it's when someone says "noice."

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.534
Tell the story of how you met
Ariana Grande

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.968
when she was 10 years old.
-So her grandma -- her nona --

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.801
brought her backstage,
and she said,

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.400
"Well, this is
my granddaughter, Ari,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.200
and she also likes to sing."

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.567
And I said, "Oh,
that's so sweet."

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.267
-And now, new stuff.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.267
These guys are so out of touch
with reality

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.634
that when House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.934
first announced the impeachment
inquiry in September,

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.534
Trump himself argued that it
would actually be good for him.

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:42.601
-I just heard that she'd like
to impeach.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.734
And I mean, if she does that,

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:47.868
they all say that's a positive
for me from the election.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.300
-Oh, do they all say that?

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.801
When you say "they," do you mean
your other personalities?

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.267
[ As Trump ] Scared Trump
says it's bad,

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.968
Sassy Trump says it's good,

00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:00.667
and Nerdy Trump says bazinga.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:09.667
-The single greatest lies ever
foistered...to de-legitimatize.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:11.434
-My favorite part of Trump's
made-up words

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.501
is how he ramps up to them
for effect

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:16.667
with a long pause,
and then gets them wrong.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.801
It's like watching one of those
dudes run up to a pool

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.067
and do a cannonball before
realizing it's frozen.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.801
[ Audience ohh's ]

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:23.934
We're also brought to you
tonight

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:26.601
by Just The Juice
Vienna Sausages.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.667
Do you love the taste
of those little sausages

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.434
that come in a jar?
Neither do we.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.133
Why we threw them out to bring
you Just the Juice.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.701
[ Audience ohh's ]

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.634
-Mmm.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.834
Tastes like a pig
took a salty bath.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:44.801
No one has ever run into
a parade and gone,

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.100
"Oh, good, a parade."
-[ Laughing ] Right.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.734
-There's always part of you
that's like,

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.567
"I hate humans."

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.667
There was that part where there
was the marching band.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.701
-Yep.
-And marching bands are --

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.133
you know, like the precision
and the rehearsal

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.501
that goes into --

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.901
You know, it's impressive
how a marching band

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.801
can take any song

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.767
and ruin it.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.667
-Right?
You're always kind of like,

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:10.701
"Wow, I didn't know I could hate
"Uptown Funk" that much.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.934
-I am a terrible procrastinator.
-Yes.

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:14.868
I think a lot of people in our
field are.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:16.033
-Whoa, yeah!
-Yeah.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:19.334
-And also at the time,
love to smoke weed.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.934
-Oh, right, right, right.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.367
So it was kind of like,
"Yeah, I'll definitely do this.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:26.200
I'll just, like, take
a quick break for one sec."

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.567
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.434
-Then, like, eight months pass
and I wake up.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.868
I'm like...[ Gasps ]

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.267
-Mouse Pads.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.534
Is your mouse becoming a woman?
Get her Mouse Pads.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:39.567
[ Music winds down ]

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.334
Amberrr!

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:50.501
The world's first vagina museum
is opening in London.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.868
-Men are allowed,

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.267
but they don't know what to do
once they get in there.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.801
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.167
What -- What -- I mean.
-Just sort of...

00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.634
Just sort of bang around, right?

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:04.501
The company Glade is currently
selling a scented candle

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:06.701
called Warm Flannel Embrace.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.367
-Warm Flannel Embrace.
Or as lesbians call it --

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.968
First Base.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.234
-I'm second-oldest of five.
-Five?!

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.400
-Yes.
-Did you guys

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.234
all treat each other
with the same respect

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.067
that those kids were treated
with on the film set?

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.534
-We did not.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.300
Worst household ever.
-Really?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.767
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:26.234
Think -- Think "Animal House."

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.534
-Okay, yeah.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:30.167
-On any given day, you could get
your ass kicked.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.400
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.467
And finally,
Family-Sized Toilets.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:37.734
Are you tired of everyone
in your house

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.701
going to the bathroom
separately?

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.567
With this massive,
12-foot-wide toilet,

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.067
there's enough room for everyone
in your family,

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.033
even grandma.

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:46.801
Finally, going to the bathroom
is an activity

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:47.934
the whole family can do
together.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.334
Family-Sized Toilets!

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.300
Because family
is number one and...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.801
number two.

